==German==

===Etymology===
<!--aus dem Obersächsischen, per Duden
-->From {{m|de|Schmetten||cream}} due to an old belief that witches transformed themselves into butterflies to steal cream and other milk products.<ref>{{R:Duden}}. / ''Duden - Deutsches Universalwörterbuch'', 4. Aufl. (Mannheim 2001)</ref> (Contrast the etymology of [[w:English language|English]] {{m|en|butterfly}}.)

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|de|/ˈʃmɛtɐlɪŋ/}}
* {{audio|de|De-Schmetterling.ogg|audio (Germany)}}

===Noun===
{{de-noun|m|Schmetterlinges|gen2=Schmetterlings|Schmetterlinge}}

# {{lb|de|chiefly|biology}} an insect of the order [[Lepidoptera]], i.e. a [[butterfly]] or [[moth]]
#: {{syn|de|Falter}}
# {{lb|de|in common use mostly}} a [[butterfly]]
#: {{syn|de|Tagfalter|Sommervogel}}
# {{lb|de|swimming}} [[butterfly]] (kind of stroke)
#: {{syn|de|Delphin}}

